      "reasoning": "It is my sixth turn. My hand is powerful but my mana has been slow to develop. My opponents have built significant board presence and resources; the Tasigur player in particular has a very full graveyard, making them a threat.\n\
\n\
My primary objective is to cast my commander, Saskia the Unyielding. She costs {R}{W}{B}{G}. I have sources for Red and Green. My `Exotic Orchard` can provide either White or Black, but not both. I am one color short.\n\
\n\
My hand contains a solution: `Grave Upheaval`. While I cannot cast this spell for its full cost, its \"Basic landcycling\" ability is my optimal play. For {2} mana, I can discard it to search my library for a basic land card and put it into my hand. This allows me to find a `Swamp`, guaranteeing I will have all four of Saskia's colors on my next turn. Cycling this card has a nearly 100% probability of setting up a successful Saskia cast on turn 7.\n\
\n\
The game state indicates that `Grave Upheaval` is \"playable\". Since I cannot afford its {6} mana cost, this must mean its cycling ability is available.\n\
\n\
My sequence for this turn will be:\n\
1.  Activate the landcycling ability of `Grave Upheaval`. I will pay the {2} cost by tapping my `Mountain` and `Forest`.\n\
2.  Search for a `Swamp` and add it to my hand.\n\
3.  With my remaining two mana, I will cast `Conqueror's Flail`.\n\
\n\
This sequence ends my turn with `Lightning Greaves` and `Conqueror's Flail` on the battlefield, and the necessary land in hand to cast a protected, hasty Saskia next turn. This is the most statistically sound line of play. I will begin by activating the cycling on `Grave Upheaval`.",
