- `GPT4om Lucky`: `Breeding Pool` untapped. (Flash deck, likely has answers).\n\
\n\
Strategic Considerations:\n\
I have `Hunter's Prowess` (5 mana). If I cast it on `Leonin Shikari` (2/2), it gets +3/+3 and trample.\n\
Eminence (Arahbo) makes it +3/+3 at start of combat? \n\
Wait, `Arahbo, Roar of the World` eminence: \"Whenever another Cat you control attacks, you may have it get +3/+3 until end of turn.\"\n\
Wait, if I cast `Hunter's Prowess` on `Leonin Shikari` and attack with it, and use eminence, it becomes 2+3+3 = 8/8 trample.\n\
If it deals damage to a player, I draw 8 cards.\n\
This is a huge turn if it resolves.\n\
However, `Managorger Hydra` will grow when I cast it. 9/9 -> 10/10.\n\
\n\
Wait, `Gem25P Stats` has `Mirror Entity`. They can activate it for X and make all their creatures X/X.\n\
They can make the Hydra huge if they have the mana.\n\
But Hydra's counters are +1/+1 counters, which add to the base stats set by Mirror Entity.\n\
So if they make base P/T 1/1, the Hydra is 1+counters. If 5/5, Hydra is 5+counters.\n\
\n\
I have `Rout` to reset if things get bad.\n\
But `Hunter's Prowess` could draw me into more answers.\n\
\n\
Let's look at `Leonin Relic-Warder`. It can exile an artifact or enchantment.\n\
- `Conqueror's Flail` (p78) - Stops opponents from casting on Gem25P's turn.\n\
- `Boompile` (p105) - 50% chance of board wipe.\n\
- `Chromatic Lantern` (p106) - Fixes mana.\n\
\n\
Exiling `Boompile` seems like a good safety play.\n\
But exiling `Conqueror's Flail` lets me use `Rout` on Gem25P's turn if they attack me for lethal.\n\
Wait, `Conqueror's Flail` rules: \"As long as {this} is attached to a creature, your opponents can't cast spells during your turn.\"\n\
Gem25P's turn. I can't cast spells while it's attached.\n\
If I remove it, I can `Rout` them if they go for the kill.\n\
\n\
Another option: `Curse of Bounty`. If I enchant `Gem25P Stats`, whenever someone attacks them, I untap my nonland permanents. \n\
With `Leonin Shikari`, that's powerful? No, it's just untapping creatures.\n\
`Curse of Vitality` - gain 2 life when player is attacked.\n\
\n\
I think the best offensive move is `Hunter's Prowess` on a Cat.\n\
If I play `Opal Palace` first, I have 7 mana. \n\
Wait, I already used 0 land drops? Yes.\n\
Play `Opal Palace`.\n\
Now 7 mana.\n\
Cast `Hunter's Prowess` (5 mana) on `Leonin Shikari`.\n\
Left: 2 mana.\n\
\n\
Wait, if I cast `Hunter's Prowess`, and `GPT4om Lucky` (Tasigur) has 7 cards and blue mana, they might counter it.\n\
Is it worth it?\n\
If it resolves, I draw many cards.\n\
If it's countered, it's 5 mana gone.\n\
\n\
Maybe I should cast `Leonin Relic-Warder` first?\n\
Wait, `Managorger Hydra` triggers on every spell.\n\
Casting `Relic-Warder` makes it 10/10.\n\
Casting `Hunter's Prowess` makes it 11/11.\n\
\n\
Wait, looking at the board:\n\
`Gem25P Stats` life: 34.\n\
`GPT4om Lucky` life: 35.\n\
`GPT52 Contra` life: 40.\n\
\n\
I should probably play the land first.\n\
Then decide on the spell.\n\
\n\
Play `Opal Palace` (p109).",
