      "reasoning": "thought Thought:\n\
\n\
GPT52 Contra's Turn 15, Precombat Main.\n\
They played Sangromancer (p211) and created an Elf Warrior token (p210).\n\
Sangromancer: \"Whenever a creature an opponent controls dies, you may gain 3 life. Whenever an opponent discards a card, you may gain 3 life.\"\n\
This is interesting. Since my hand is empty, I'm not discarding.\n\
But if I kill their creatures later, they gain life... wait, no. \"Whenever a creature an OPPONENT controls dies\". I am the opponent.\n\
So if MY cats die, they gain life.\n\
My cats are not dying easily (Double strike + protection from Rats).\n\
\n\
They have Whispersilk Cloak (p188).\n\
If they equip it to Nath or Sangromancer, that creature becomes a threat.\n\
Nath is a 4/4.\n\
I have a huge board, but no flyers except the Spirit of the Hearth that I FAILED TO CAST.\n\
Wait, I keep saying I failed to cast Spirit of the Hearth.\n\
Let's look at my graveyard.\n\
\"Spirit of the Hearth (p206) is in the graveyard.\"\n\
Why?\n\
Maybe during the \"Unknown\" choice I somehow discarded it?\n\
Or did it get countered?\n\
Actually, if I called pass_priority instead of choose_action earlier, did I effectively skip my turn?\n\
Regardless, it's there.\n\
\n\
Current situation:\n\
Contra has 9 life.\n\
I have 29 life.\n\
My turn is next.\n\
If I survive and attack, I win.\n\
The only way they stop me is a board wipe or a very efficient set of blockers.\n\
They have a bunch of Zombies and 2 Rats and an Elf.\n\
They have shroud on one Zombie token (p172).\n\
\n\
I have Leonin Shikari and Hero's Blade.\n\
Hero's Blade is not equipped to anything?\n\
Wait, if it's on the battlefield, it's not equipped.\n\
