      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Destroying Sol Ring on turn 3 is a reasonable tempo play, generating two 1/1 Saproling tokens. However, this uses the Artifact Mutation early when there's no pressing need — Sol Ring has already been used this turn (it's tapped), and GPT52 Contra only has Wall of Blossoms as a creature (a defensive 0/4). The two 1/1 tokens aren't particularly impactful in a 4-player game. Meanwhile, Gem25P Stats is spending their turn 3 on removing a mana rock rather than developing their own board. Holding Artifact Mutation for a higher-value artifact later (like Dreamstone Hedron which would generate 6 tokens) or keeping mana open for Boros Charm or Crackling Doom as interaction could be more valuable. That said, denying Sol Ring's mana advantage early is a valid strategy, making this debatable rather than clearly wrong.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Artifact Mutation targeting Sol Ring (CMC 1), destroying it and creating one 1/1 Saproling token.",
      "better_line": "Play Terramorphic Expanse as a land drop (if not already played) and pass the turn, holding up Artifact Mutation for a potentially higher-value target later, or saving mana for reactive plays like Boros Charm or Crackling Doom.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 104,
      "player": "Gem25P Stats",
      "decision_index": 35,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Dreamstone Hedron (6 mana) uses all available mana this turn, deploying a ramp artifact when there are no immediate threats to answer. Meanwhile, Alms Collector (3/4 flash) could be held up as a surprise play, and Stalking Leonin (3/3 for 3) provides early board presence. The Hedron is a reasonable ramp play with Temple of the False God active, but playing it now means no mana left for interaction. Alternatively, playing Tranquil Thicket as a land drop first (tapped land) and then casting Stalking Leonin or Alms Collector would develop the board while keeping options open. However, the player hasn't played their land for the turn yet - they have Forest and Tranquil Thicket in hand but chose to cast Dreamstone Hedron before playing a land, which is a minor sequencing issue since they could play Forest untapped first to have 7 mana available (though Hedron costs exactly 6). The bigger concern is that Dreamstone Hedron is slow ramp in a multiplayer game where developing board presence or holding up interaction might be more valuable at this stage.",
