      "description": "Attacking the highest-life player (Gem3F Proud at 41hp) instead of the most vulnerable player (GPT4om Lucky at 35hp with minimal board presence). Both have no available blockers, so full 6 damage connects either way. Attacking Lucky would pressure the weakest player more effectively, following the typical multiplayer strategy of eliminating opponents.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked Gem3F Proud (41hp) with 6/6 Managorger Hydra",
      "better_line": "Attack GPT4om Lucky (35hp, fewest permanents, no blockers) to pressure the most vulnerable opponent toward elimination",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 362,
      "player": "Gem25P Stats",
      "decision_index": 185,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "When ordering cards on the bottom of library from Abundance, the player chose to put Nazahn, Revered Bladesmith (their best card among the three, being a Cat that tutors equipment and synergizes with their equipment theme) on the very bottom, making it least accessible. Leonin Arbiter is a weak 2/2 with a search-taxing ability that could hurt their own plans.",
      "action_taken": "Ordered cards with Leonin Arbiter closest to top and Nazahn deepest on bottom",
      "better_line": "Put Leonin Arbiter on the very bottom (choose last) and keep Nazahn closer to accessible, as Nazahn synergizes strongly with the equipment/Cat theme on board (Grappling Hook, Leonin Shikari, Sunspear Shikari, Arahbo commander)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 373,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 197,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Hunter's Prowess is a sorcery-speed pump spell (+3/+3, trample, draw cards on combat damage) that needs to target a creature before combat. The likely target is Sunspear Shikari (2/2) or Leonin Shikari (2/2), making them 5/5. However, casting it before combat telegraphs the plan. More importantly, Gem25P Stats has a Managorger Hydra with 6 +1/+1 counters (7/7) that will get another counter from this spell cast, and Mirror Entity which could pump the whole team. The Prowess target could be chump-blocked by Wall of Blossoms or other creatures. Also, Leonin Relic-Warder could exile Conqueror's Flail or Chromatic Lantern, which provides more lasting board impact. Casting Hunter's Prowess risks the creature being removed before combat (though GPT4om Lucky has only 3 untapped lands - Breeding Pool - and most removal is in graveyard). The play isn't terrible since drawing cards off combat damage would be very valuable, but casting Leonin Relic-Warder first to exile a key artifact, then potentially using remaining mana for Curse of Bounty or saving for next turn's Rout might be more strategic given the threatening Managorger Hydra board state.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Hunter's Prowess for 5 mana targeting one of their small cats",
      "better_line": "Consider casting Leonin Relic-Warder to exile Conqueror's Flail (preventing Gem25P Stats from locking out opponents on their turn) and saving mana/cards, or holding up for Rout next turn to deal with the growing Managorger Hydra threat. Alternatively, cast Curse of Bounty on an opponent to set up future value.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 375,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 199,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Hunter's Prowess gives +3/+3, trample, and 'draw cards equal to combat damage dealt' to the target. Targeting Leonin Shikari (2/2, becomes 5/5) instead of Sunspear Shikari (2/2, becomes 5/5 with lifelink if equipped) is suboptimal, but the real blunder is not targeting the Managorger Hydra. The Hydra is a 9/9 (1/1 base + 6 counters + 2 from additional spells cast) that becomes 12/12 with trample and card draw on combat damage. With Grappling Hook equipped (double strike + forced block), the Hydra could deal massive damage and draw a huge number of cards. However, the Hydra belongs to Gem25P Stats (an opponent), not to Gem3F Proud. Looking more carefully: Hunter's Prowess targets 'target creature' - it can target any creature. The Hydra is an opponent's creature, so giving it +3/+3 and card draw would be terrible. Among Gem3F Proud's own creatures (Leonin Shikari and Sunspear Shikari), Sunspear Shikari is equipped with nothing currently, but Grappling Hook is on the battlefield. If Grappling Hook is equipped to Sunspear Shikari, it gets double strike and lifelink (from being equipped), making it a 5/5 double strike lifelink trample that draws cards equal to combat damage - potentially 10 cards and 10 life. Leonin Shikari has the ability to equip at instant speed but doesn't benefit from being equipped itself. Targeting Leonin Shikari (5/5 trample, draw cards) vs Sunspear Shikari (5/5 trample + can be equipped with Grappling Hook for double strike + lifelink, drawing potentially 10 cards) is significantly worse.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Leonin Shikari with Hunter's Prowess, making it a 5/5 with trample and card draw.",
      "better_line": "Target Sunspear Shikari with Hunter's Prowess, then equip Grappling Hook to it for double strike and lifelink (from Sunspear Shikari's ability), creating a 5/5 double strike trample lifelink creature that could draw up to 10 cards on combat damage and gain 10 life. Leonin Shikari's instant-speed equip ability enables this line perfectly.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 376,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 204,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Proud is casting Leonin Shikari (costs {1}{W}) and needs to activate Opal Palace for mana. They chose option 1 ({T}: Add {C}) which produces colorless mana. However, option 2 ({1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity) would produce a colored mana and give their commander an additional +1/+1 counter when cast from the command zone later. Since Leonin Shikari costs {1}{W}, they need one white and one generic. They have Plains untapped (for {W}), Temple of the False God untapped (for {C}{C} with 10 lands), Vivid Grove untapped, and Opal Palace. Either option works to cast the Shikari, but option 2 costs {1} more to activate - requiring spending an additional mana. Looking more carefully: they have Plains, Temple of the False God, Vivid Grove, and Opal Palace untapped (4 lands). Leonin Shikari costs {1}{W}. Using Opal Palace option 1 gives {C}, Plains gives {W} - that's exactly {1}{W}. Using option 2 would cost {1} + {T} from Opal Palace, so they'd need to tap another land just to activate it, then get one colored mana. That would use 3 lands for what option 1 does in 2. However, with Mirari's Wake on the battlefield, each land tapped for mana adds an additional mana. So Plains tapped produces {W}{W}, Temple produces {C}{C}{C}{C}, Opal Palace option 1 produces {C}{C}, Vivid Grove produces {G}{G}. They have massive mana available. Using option 2 would cost {1} from another source + tap Opal Palace to get a colored mana + commander counter benefit. With Mirari's Wake, they have plenty of spare mana. The commander counter benefit is minor but free value they're leaving on the table - though they'd need to spend 1 extra mana to activate option 2. With abundant mana available this is a very minor optimization miss.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Opal Palace for {C} (option 1)",
      "better_line": "Activate Opal Palace option 2 ({1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color in commander's color identity) to bank the commander counter benefit for a future Arahbo cast, using spare mana from Temple of the False God or Vivid Grove to pay the {1} activation cost",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 550,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 306,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Sunspear Shikari before playing the Forest in hand. With Mirari's Wake on the battlefield, playing the Forest first would generate additional mana (Forest would tap for GG with Wake). This extra mana could be used to activate Krosan Verge or put storage counters on Saltcrusted Steppe. Additionally, casting a creature pre-combat is slightly suboptimal when they could attack with Leonin Shikari first (getting Arahbo's eminence +3/+3 trigger).",
      "action_taken": "Cast Sunspear Shikari without first playing the Forest from hand.",
      "better_line": "Play Forest first (gaining extra mana from Mirari's Wake), then consider entering combat to use Arahbo's eminence trigger on Leonin Shikari, then cast Sunspear Shikari post-combat, and use remaining mana to activate Krosan Verge for further ramp to prepare for the incoming zombie army.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 587,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 329,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Proud has Krosan Verge untapped and a Plains untapped (which produces WW with Mirari's Wake, enough to pay the {2} activation cost). Activating Krosan Verge to fetch a Forest and Plains onto the battlefield is pure value - trading one land for two lands, which are even better with Mirari's Wake doubling mana. Especially important facing 13 Zombie tokens from GPT52 Contra that will attack next turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without activating Krosan Verge or casting any spells.",
      "better_line": "Activate Krosan Verge (tap it, pay {2} from Plains with Mirari's Wake, sacrifice Krosan Verge) to search for a Forest and Plains, ramping from the current land count and increasing future mana production with Mirari's Wake.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 588,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 330,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "GPT52 Contra just resolved Army of the Damned creating 13 zombie tokens (26 power) that will untap and attack next turn. Contra is the clear primary threat. Both opponents have no blockers, so the attack is free either way. Attacking Contra reduces their life total and applies pressure to the biggest threat.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked GPT4om Lucky (27hp) with Leonin Shikari instead of the player with 13 zombie tokens.",
      "better_line": "Attack GPT52 Contra to apply pressure to the biggest threat on board - the player with 13 zombies about to untap.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 590,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 334,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Proud declined to activate Krosan Verge when they had exactly enough mana to do so (Krosan Verge tap + Plains producing double mana via Mirari's Wake). This would have fetched a Forest and Plains onto the battlefield, providing permanent ramp especially valuable with Mirari's Wake doubling all land production. Facing 13 zombie tokens threatening to attack next turn, maximizing mana development is critical for casting answers.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without activating Krosan Verge or casting any spell.",
      "better_line": "Activate Krosan Verge (tap it + tap Plains for WW via Mirari's Wake to pay the {2} cost) to search for a Forest and Plains, increasing land count and future mana production significantly with Mirari's Wake on the battlefield.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 596,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 339,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Gave the Rat token to GPT4om Lucky (the weaker opponent at 21 life with almost no board) instead of GPT52 Contra (the dominant threat with 13 Zombie tokens at 33 life). Giving the Rat to Contra could potentially lead to it dying sooner in combat interactions, which would trigger +1/+1 counters on all Cats. Additionally, giving resources to the weaker player is generally less desirable than giving them to the player you need to pressure.",
      "action_taken": "Chose GPT4om Lucky to receive the Rat token from Hungry Lynx's trigger",
      "better_line": "Give the Rat token to GPT52 Contra, the biggest threat with 13 Zombie tokens, where the Rat is more likely to die in combat and trigger Cat +1/+1 counters",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 596,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 339,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Tapped Saltcrusted Steppe for colorless mana to cast Raksha Golden Cub when they likely had more than enough mana from other lands with Mirari's Wake doubling. With 2 Plains (4W) and Temple of the False God (4C), that's already 8 mana for a 7-mana spell. Keeping Saltcrusted Steppe untapped would allow adding a storage counter with spare mana later in the turn.",
      "action_taken": "Tapped Saltcrusted Steppe for {C} to help pay for Raksha Golden Cub",
      "better_line": "Leave Saltcrusted Steppe untapped and use other lands (Plains, Temple of the False God, etc.) which with Mirari's Wake produce more than enough mana, then use spare mana to add a storage counter to Saltcrusted Steppe",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 618,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 353,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "By activating Krosan Verge precombat, Gem3F Proud spends their last 2 untapped mana (Plains + Forest, which with Mirari's Wake would produce WWGG = 4 mana). This means they cannot pay {1}{G}{W} for Arahbo's combat pump trigger when a Cat attacks. The pump gives +X/+X and trample where X is the creature's power, which could be significant damage against GPT52 Contra's tapped zombie board.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Krosan Verge during precombat main, using all remaining untapped mana to fetch two tapped lands.",
      "better_line": "Save Krosan Verge activation for after combat (or second main phase). Use the untapped Plains and Forest (doubled by Mirari's Wake to WWGG) to pay {1}{G}{W} for Arahbo's pump trigger on an attacking Cat, pushing more damage through against the tapped zombie tokens.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 623,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 363,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem3F Proud attacked for only 20 damage against GPT52 Contra's 21 life, missing lethal. They have Hero's Blade in hand and Leonin Shikari on the battlefield (allowing instant-speed equip). Casting Hero's Blade (2 mana) in main phase 1 and equipping it to Raksha Golden Cub (4 mana) would make Raksha equipped, triggering Raksha's ability giving ALL cats +2/+2 and double strike. With Mirari's Wake doubling mana, they easily had the 6 mana needed. Double strike on all four attacking cats would have dealt far more than 21 damage for a clean lethal kill.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with all 4 creatures for 20 total damage against opponent at 21 life, without casting Hero's Blade first.",
      "better_line": "In main phase 1, cast Hero's Blade (2 mana), then equip to Raksha Golden Cub (4 mana, instant-speed via Leonin Shikari). This gives all cats +2/+2 and double strike, resulting in lethal damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 658,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 385,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chose not to block a 2/2 Zombie Token when multiple 4/4 creatures were available to block and kill it with no risk. Taking 2 unnecessary damage at 29 life in a 1v1 situation against an opponent with 9 life and a large zombie army.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to block the attacking 2/2 Zombie Token, taking 2 damage (29 -> 27 life).",
      "better_line": "Block with any of the 4/4 creatures (Leonin Shikari, Hungry Lynx, or Sunspear Shikari) to kill the zombie and preserve life total. Every point of life matters when facing 10+ zombie tokens.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 678,
      "player": "Gem3F Proud",
      "decision_index": 398,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Proud has cats with protection from Rats (due to Hungry Lynx) and Raksha Golden Cub giving all cats double strike (since Hero's Blade is on the battlefield as equipment). With 4 attackers incoming (2 Zombie 2/2 tokens and 2 Rat 1/1 tokens), they only blocked 2 of the 4 attackers, letting a Zombie Token through for 2 damage. They have plenty of creatures available to block all attackers - Leonin Shikari, Hungry Lynx, Sunspear Shikari, and Raksha Golden Cub could each block one attacker. Additionally, the cats have protection from Rats so the Rat tokens can't even deal damage to them, and with Sunspear Shikari having lifelink + double strike, blocking maximizes life gain. Taking 2 unnecessary damage when at 29 life against an opponent at 9 life with a board full of zombies is meaningful.",
      "action_taken": "Only blocked 2 of 4 attackers (Sunspear Shikari blocked a Rat Token, left a Zombie Token unblocked), taking 2 unnecessary damage.",
      "better_line": "Block all 4 attackers: Leonin Shikari blocks a Zombie, Hungry Lynx blocks a Zombie, Sunspear Shikari blocks a Rat, Raksha Golden Cub blocks the other Rat. This prevents all combat damage and gains life from Sunspear Shikari's lifelink.",
